+-- !-- Lab Notebook: fibEntryPt_mul_coprime -- !--
+-- !-- Hypothesis: for coprime a,b the apparition index of the product is lcm of the parts' indices, i.e. α is "multiplicative up to lcm" on coprime inputs. -- !--
+-- !-- Result: Proved (sorry = 0).  The product ab inherits an entry point at L = lcm(α a, α b), and the index set of ab is exactly the multiples of L. -- !--
+-- !-- Insight: The characterization theorem `fib_dvd_iff_entryPt_dvd` holds for ARBITRARY moduli (never used primality), so it applies to a, b AND ab simultaneously; coprimality turns `ab ∣ F k` into `a ∣ F k ∧ b ∣ F k`, and `Nat.lcm_dvd_iff` collapses the conjunction of ideals into a single ideal generated by the lcm. -- !--
+-- !-- Failure analysis: The only subtlety is establishing that ab HAS an entry point before invoking the characterization; this needs the explicit witness L = lcm(α a, α b) together with `Nat.Coprime.mul_dvd_of_dvd_of_dvd`. -- !--
+-- !-- End Lab Notebook -- !--
+-/
 theorem fibEntryPt_mul_coprime {a b : ℕ}
     (hab : Nat.Coprime a b)
     (ha : ∃ k, 0 < k ∧ a ∣ Nat.fib k) (hb : ∃ k, 0 < k ∧ b ∣ Nat.fib k) :
     fibEntryPt (a * b) = Nat.lcm (fibEntryPt a) (fibEntryPt b) := by
